# Hardware shared by the scenarios - matches the default config.h: three local loads on D5-D7,
# override pin D4. The board (its analog inputs, ADC reference, calibration and mains) comes from
# the board file, read after the scenario (board_scn.sh, grid_sim -b): the same scenarios run on
# the three boards.

# load <pin> <W>: physicalLoadPin[] = { 5, 6, 7 }, priorities 0, 1, 2. CT2 measures the three.
load 5 1000
load 6 1000
load 7 1000

# D4 is the override pin (active LOW): keep it released
input 4 1

# Conversions filed under the wrong channel (an ISR longer than one conversion breaks ADMUX's
# two-conversion pipeline): none allowed.
expect misfiled_samples 0
# ADMUX must change one ADC clock (128 cycles) or more after the conversion started
expect admux_delay_min 128
# The ISR must end within the 1664 cycles of one conversion
expect isr_overruns 0
# Margins, enforced: the longest ISR call and the latest ADMUX write (from the interrupt), a little
# above the worst of the builds (495 and 1456 cycles). The deadline is 1664 cycles: an ADMUX written
# later misses the conversion after next, which then converts the wrong channel. The latest writes
# are those of the builds with temperature sensing: a 1-Wire time slot keeps interrupts off up to
# ~65 us (~1050 cycles), and the ISR entered that late still has to reach its ADMUX write (~420
# cycles at most: the work of the mains cycle is spread over the CT2 calls, processing.cpp).
# admux_delay_max leaves room for the ordinary shifts of the 1-Wire slots against the ADC phase: a
# failure between 1620 and 1664 with misfiled_samples 0 is a margin warning, not a lost sample.
expect isr_max 560
expect admux_delay_max 1620
# no sample beyond the ADC's range
expect clipped 0
